    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d453-a1">

                <pb facs="0612" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg298"/>


                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr</hi>. 
                        <hi rendition="#italic">J. L’Engle</hi>
                    
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to Senator</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>
                    
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Jacksonville, Florida</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 27, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Newspapers report that British Government has announced intention permit cotton
                    shipments direct to Germany; our people regard it very important to secure right
                    guaranteed by similar declaration to ship naval stores to Germany as part of
                    cotton cargoes. Naval stores shipments necessary ballast for cotton cargoes. I
                    understand that neither cotton nor naval stores are contraband of war and we
                    would be greatly obliged if you would ask State Department to secure declaration
                    from British Ambassador to this effect in order facilitate joint shipments of
                    naval stores and cotton from Atlantic and Gulf ports direct to Germany. If this
                    assurance can be secured it will constitute important and far-reaching measure
                    of relief to naval stores industry. Please answer.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. J. L’Engle</hi>
                    
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
